 ],
 "text": "Two bugs just left a lot of online stores wide open. They're called PHP-to-shell, and they let anyone take over a web server without a password. The fix came out on October 21, but Amazon saw a tax a week before that. About 70% of the web runs on PHP, including WordPress. So do three things today. Ask your host if PHP was patched after October 21. Update your store, your plugins, and your themes. And look for admin users nobody created. Want the full check? Comment Systems and we'll send it to you free."
